                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The patient’s estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) is mildly decreased (67 mL/min/1.73 m²), consistent with stage 2 chronic kidney disease, which is common in elderly individuals. No acute kidney injury is indicated. Continued monitoring of renal function is recommended, especially if comorbidities or nephrotoxic medications are present.</td>
